{
  "version": 1,
  "about": [
    "Curated drive-family specifications. Consulted BEFORE the title regexes, and",
    "raises confidence when it hits, because a family name is far more reliable",
    "evidence than a token in a seller-written title.",
    "",
    "CMR/SMR is the field that matters most and the field almost never stated in a",
    "listing. It decides whether a drive survives a RAID rebuild, so a wrong value",
    "here is exactly the kind of wrong number CLAUDE.md §1.1 is about.",
    "",
    "Fields are omitted rather than guessed. A family that genuinely ships in both",
    "SATA and SAS (Exos, Ultrastar) has no `interface`, and the title regex decides.",
    "A family with mixed recording technology across capacities (WD Blue 3.5\", WD",
    "Red non-Plus, Toshiba P300) carries `technologyConfidence` BELOW the 0.6",
    "publish threshold, so those listings quarantine unless the title states CMR/SMR",
    "outright or a specific model number in this file resolves them. That is",
    "deliberate: coverage is not the metric.",
    "",
    "`confidence` applies to every field the entry supplies; a per-axis override",
    "(`technologyConfidence`, `formFactorConfidence`, `interfaceConfidence`) narrows",
    "it for one axis. Longer `match` strings win over shorter ones, so",
    "'ironwolf pro' beats 'ironwolf' and a model number beats a family name."
  ],
